                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9781351251624"} doi:10.1201/9781351251624
          %p A lightning review of results by Henn with Goerss, Mahowald, Rezk, and Karamanov:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans-Werner+Henn"}> Hans-Werner Henn
              ,
              %em Recent developments in chromatic stable homotopy theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://etale.site/livetex/saft/henn.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack
          %p A collection of various lecture notes and other material is kept at
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/index.php?year=2013"}> Talbot 2013: Chromatic Homotopy Theory
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.hiroleetanaka.com/pretalbot2013/index.php"} 2013 Pre-Talbot Seminar Chromatic homotopy theoy
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Glossary for stable and chromatic honotopy theory (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/StableChromaticGlossary.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Mehrle18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Mehrle"}> David Mehrle
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chromatic homotopy theory: Journey to the frontier
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://pi.math.cornell.edu/~dmehrle/notes/conferences/cht/cht-notes.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Mehrle_ChromaticHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            to higher chromatic homotopy theory is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doug+Ravenel"}> Doug Ravenel
                ,
                %em Toward higher chromatic analogs of elliptic cohomology
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/mypapers/high1.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doug+Ravenel"}> Doug Ravenel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Toward higher chromatic analogs of elliptic cohomology II
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/mypapers/high2.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/mypapers/halifax.pdf"} pdf slides
          %p
            Relation of chromatic homotopy theory to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+calculus"} Goodwillie calculus
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Arone"}> Greg Arone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Mahowald"} Mark Mahowald
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Goodwillie tower of the identity functor and the unstable periodic homotopy of spheres
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Arone-Mahowald/ArMahowald.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s002220050300"} doi:10.1007/s002220050300
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Kuhn"}> Nicholas Kuhn
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Goodwillie towers and chromatic homotopy: an overview
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0410342"} arXiv:math/0410342
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/gtm.2007.10.245"} doi:10.2140/gtm.2007.10.245
          %p
            Categorical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultraproducts"} ultraproducts
            are used to provide asymptotic approximations in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Barthel"}> Tobias Barthel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomer+Schlank"} Tomer Schlank
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathaniel+Stapleton"} Nathaniel Stapleton
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chromatic homotopy theory is asymptotically algebraic
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.00844"} arXiv:1711.00844
          %p
            A form of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+program"} Langlands program
            for chromatic homotopy theory is sketched in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doron+Grossman-Naples"}> Doron Grossman-Naples
              ,
              %em Towards a chromatic Langlands program
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doronlgn.github.io/TalkNotes/TowardsChromaticLanglands.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#unstable_case Unstable case
          %p
            There are also chromatic approximations in ordinary (not
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilized
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aldridge+Bousfield"}> Aldridge Bousfield
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Localization and periodicity in unstable homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0894-0347-1994-1257059-7"} doi:10.1090/S0894-0347-1994-1257059-7
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2152734"} jstor:2152734
            %li#Heuts18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+Heuts"}> Gijs Heuts
                ,
                %em
                  Lie algebras and
                  = succeed "-periodic" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_n
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.06325"}> arXiv:1803.06325
                )
            %li#LurieHopkins18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Unstable Chromatic Homotopy Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.harvard.edu/~lurie/Thursday2017.html"} web
        .revisedby
